prompts.template:
`${header}
SOURCE SEGMENT ${index + 1} OF ${chunks}. Interpret this segment; do not claim to have seen unprovided segments. Inventory: ${JSON.stringify(profile.inventory)}
${retainedSource.slice(index * CHUNK_SIZE, (index + 1) * CHUNK_SIZE)}
Analyze the actual source organization. In headers, include source positions when available (e.g. C8 항목). Include all separate regions, even when criteria are split across sheets, columns or blank rows. Explain uncertainty rather than guessing.`

`DOCUMENT_ID ${document.id}
INVENTORY ${JSON.stringify(profile.inventory)}
PROPOSED_ANALYSIS ${JSON.stringify(context)}
ORIGINAL_SOURCE_SEGMENT ${index + 1}/${segments}
${source.slice(index * SOURCE_CHUNK, (index + 1) * SOURCE_CHUNK)}`

`Repair the COMPLETE prior structure analysis using the freshly reread original source. Preserve correct regions and add omitted ones. Resolve questions only when supported by actual source; retain genuine ambiguity. Use sheet cell ranges and exact header addresses/text, Word ranges BLOCK1:BLOCK4, and text L1:L20 where applicable. Output the complete replacement analysis, not a patch.
DOCUMENT_ID ${document.id}
INVENTORY ${JSON.stringify(profile.inventory)}
PRIOR_ANALYSIS ${JSON.stringify(context)}
VERIFICATION_ISSUES ${JSON.stringify(issues)}
FRESH_ORIGINAL_SOURCE ${JSON.stringify(evidence.selections)}`

`Independently compare the original visuals with the entire structured transcription below. Inspect ONLY actual original page positions (1-based): ${requestedPages.join(', ')}. ${expectedPages ? `The independently supplied file page count is ${expectedPages}.` : 'The total file page count is unverified; do not infer it from a filename or printed pagination.'}
Document kind: ${document.kind}. ${document.kind !== 'pdf' ? 'A standalone image is exactly page 1 of the supplied source even when its printed pagination mentions other pages.' : 'Use the actual positions in the supplied original PDF, not printed page numbers.'}
Any explicitly labelled server-rendered PDF page images show the same original page positions, never additional pages. Inspect those renderings when the PDF viewer omits glyphs because of font rendering. Keep every finding attached to its labelled original page, and retain uncertainty if neither representation is readable.
Check EVERY requested page, including its top title and metadata, all column and row headers, side labels, all table cells, units, footnotes, and readable stamps. Verify reading order, page rotation, multi-column layout, merged cells, and tables nested inside cells. Distinguish real nested tables from a multi-row header or adjacent independent tables. The transcription must retain the visible source structure, not just selected result values. Do not treat complete=true as evidence of completion.
Compare exact values, decimal zeros, commas, inequality signs, ranges, ND and other qualitative results. Check row/column alignment and links between parent cells and nested tables. Do not normalize, translate, invent obscured characters, or fill blanks. A missing requested page, unreadable region, ambiguous alignment, uncertain glyph, omitted heading/table/note, incorrect rotation/reading order, or discrepancy must be an issue with its actual requested page number. If you cannot inspect or reliably compare a region, preserve that uncertainty as an issue and explain the limit; never approve by assumption.
Return acceptable=true only when ALL requested pages have been visually inspected and no unresolved issue or verification limit remains. issues contains specific {page,detail} findings; rereadPages lists requested pages needing another reading. If a requested page has an entirely empty transcription, approve it ONLY if the original is actually blank and blankPages includes {page,reason} with a concrete explanation that you inspected its whole visible area. Blank cells or a blank transcription alone never prove a blank page. A page with grid lines, a title, stamps, or any other meaningful visible content is not blank. Use blankPages only for actually blank originals with empty transcripts. verificationLimits is optional and contains unresolved inspection limits, not generic disclaimers. Do not return repaired text, verdicts about the document's subject matter, or pages outside the requested set.
BEGIN UNTRUSTED TRANSCRIPTION JSON
${JSON.stringify({ pages })}
END UNTRUSTED TRANSCRIPTION JSON`
